  "details": "When one uses cameras on avatars, if the camera sees an object with a grab pass it emits the following error:\nWarning    -  RenderTexture.Create: Depth|ShadowMap RenderTexture requested without a depth buffer. Changing to a 16 bit depth buffer.\nFor worlds, we can use \nCamDepthBottom.SetTargetBuffers( rtDepthThrowawayColor.colorBuffer, TheActualDepthBuffer.depthBuffer );\nIn order to prevent the following error from happening because it has a regular texture bound, but for avatars, there's no mechanism to bind a throw away color buffer.  Could you scan for cameras on avatars, create a dummy render texture for the width/height and bind it using the above code?",
